\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Theorem}
\title{The Feynman–Kac kernel}
\date{2026-11-09}

\p{For the Hamiltonian of \ref{fdip-00H2}, let
#{\alpha:[0,1]\to\mathbb R^V} be the centered continuous Gaussian
bridge with covariance form
##{\begin{gathered}
\mathbb E[\langle u,\alpha(r)\rangle\langle v,\alpha(t)\rangle]
 =(\min(r,t)-rt)\langle u,v\rangle,\\
u,v\in\mathbb R^V,\qquad r,t\in[0,1].
\end{gathered}}
For #{t>0}, set
##{\begin{aligned}
X_r^{x,y}&=(1-r/t)x+(r/t)y+\sqrt t\,\alpha(r/t),\quad 0\le r\le t,\\
K_t(x,y)&=p_t(x-y)\,
 \mathbb E\exp\left(-\int_0^t U(X_r^{x,y})\,dr\right).
\end{aligned}}
Then #{K_t} is a strictly positive, continuous, symmetric kernel
for #{\ue^{-tH}}, and
##{0<K_t(x,y)\le \ue^{bt}p_t(x-y).}
In particular, the semigroup improves positivity.}

\proof{
\p{Choose an orthonormal basis of #{\mathbb R^V} for applying the
Euclidean kernel theorem. In this basis the bridge coordinates are
independent standard scalar bridges, since their joint Gaussian
covariance is #{\delta_{ij}(\min(r,t)-rt)}.
The potential is real, continuous and bounded below.
The core argument of \ref{fdip-00H2} identifies its form
Hamiltonian with the Schrödinger realization in
\citet{Theorem 1.1, (1.1)-(1.3), p. 2}{simon1999feynman}.
That theorem uses exactly #{-\covsq /2}, the stated bridge
covariance and the prefactor #{(2\pi t)^{-s/2}}, so it gives
the asserted integral kernel.}

\p{Each bridge path is continuous with compact range. The
potential along it is bounded, so its exponential integral is
finite and strictly positive. The lower bound #{U\ge-b}
gives the common majorant #{\ue^{bt}}. For convergent endpoints,
continuity of #{U} gives uniform convergence along a fixed bridge
path on a common compact range. Dominated convergence proves
endpoint continuity; bridge reversal proves symmetry.
The Gaussian bound gives square-integrable kernel sections,
hence pointwise representatives of semigroup outputs. Integrating
a strictly positive kernel against a nonnegative nonzero function
proves positivity improvement.}
}
